this is the moment alexander cardinale  finally held his biological daughter  four months after she was born  but to meet this little girl he had to  give away a child that he and his wife  had already bonded with losing the birth  child that you know  for the genetic child that you don't  even know yet  it's a truly impossible nightmare  and daphne had to accept that the baby  she carried for nine months was not  biologically hers  instead of breastfeeding my own child  i breastfed and bonded with a child i  was later forced to give away the  cardinales are suing their fertility  doctor illeran moore they're also some  in his clinic his lab and the surgical  center where the ivf procedure took  place back in 2019  the couple's despair began in the  delivery room when they were given a  child they didn't recognize and who  looked nothing like their older daughter  a genetic test at three months old  revealed the child was not theirs  the embryo had been switched with  another couple the children born just a  week apart  the couple's lawyer says the  multi-billion dollar fertility industry  needs more regulation  fertility centers are almost entirely  unregulated  barber shops and nail salons are subject  to far tighter state and federal  regulation fertility experts dispute  this  we're inspected every two years by the  college of american pathologists these  are high-end inspections they look at  every single detail of every single  procedure that goes on as for the  cardinalis they say they're still  adjusting to raising a new child  the daughter we raised and bonded with  was gone  after months of love and affection  the lawsuit won't reverse their grief or  buy back precious moments lost but they  hope it could save others the heartbreak  schmann freeman powell sky news
 

